{
  "_comment": [
    "Pages the web UI smoke check loads (#5701). Every page gets the same checks (smoke.mjs): no console error, page error, failed request or /api/* answer >= 400; #main fills; the sidebar lists the seeded servers; the nav link for the route is active; no .strip.error or [role=alert]; no panel still loading or in error.",
    "Per page, 'expect' adds what the seed guarantees. A panel is found by its data-panel (the read name) or its data-title; data-panel is unambiguous only for a read that feeds one card, so key a fanout panel (several cards sharing one read) by title; 'state' is data (draws rows, a chart or tiles) or empty (shows its documented empty text); 'minRows' counts the rows of the first [data-grid] inside it. 'grids' does the same for the whole page (an Admin tab has no panel cards): 'minRows' or 'exactRows' on the Nth [data-grid] in #main.",
    "screenshot: a page with this key also gets a baseline PNG (shots.mjs, #5744; tools/ui-smoke/baselines/<name>.png). Its mask is a list of CSS selectors painted over before the compare, added to screenshotDefaults.mask (the status bar clock, the refresh hint, a chart tooltip): put in it anything whose text changes from run to run.",
    "allowList: a console or request message that is known and harmless. Each entry needs an 'issue' number and a 'match' substring. It starts empty."
  ],
  "screenshotDefaults": {
    "mask": ["#statusbar .sb-updated", "#refresh-hint", ".chart-tooltip"]
  },
  "allowList": [],
